          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-02T04:11:29-07:00",
          "message": "fix(daemon): the draw's reserve holds a draw descheduled on a busy machine (candybar-launch-q7o7.qjw) (#560)\n\n* fix(daemon): the draw's reserve holds a draw descheduled on a busy machine (candybar-launch-q7o7.qjw)\n\nOn CI's runner, its cores shared with the other process-tier suites, a cold\ndraw that does a few ms of work reads up to 48 ms of wall time, failing the\n40 ms reserve. Reproduced locally with every core busy: median 2 ms, p99 48 ms.\nA larger reserve costs only more pending values; a smaller one blanks the bar.\n\n* docs(daemon): keep the user-config figure behind the draw reserve; process runs land within it (candybar-launch-q7o7.qjw)\n\n* docs(daemon): the draw reserve's comment claims no user-config coverage; process margin stays thin (candybar-launch-q7o7.qjw)\n\n* test(daemon): the held client's stated budget follows the draw reserve (candybar-launch-q7o7.qjw)"
        }
      ]
    },
